78	/**
79	 * The line a person reads under the two tags.
80	 *
81	 * GitHub renders neither tag, so a body of tags alone reaches the page as an empty
82	 * comment — a run announcing itself looked like a comment somebody had posted and
83	 * left blank (#349). The tags are the record and must stay; this is the part a
84	 * person sees, written in the shape the dispatch marker uses for the same reason.
85	 * It carries no tag and no `/agent` command: prose that read as either would move
86	 * the turn this comment exists to name.
87	 */
88	const CLAIM_NOTICE = "Atomaton: claimed this turn.";
